// ROOT package.json: the workspace "orchestrator". It isn't an app itself.
//
// ⚠️  JSON doesn't allow comments. Delete ALL of these lines once you've
//     written the real content, or pnpm won't parse the file.
//
// Fields to write:
//
//   "name"            Any name, e.g. "the-jejune-agency". It's never published.
//
//   "private": true   REQUIRED at the root of a workspace. It stops anyone from
//                     accidentally running `npm publish` on the whole monorepo.
//
//   "packageManager"  "pnpm@<version>". Pins the pnpm version so Corepack (which
//                     ships with Node) and CI use the same one. Your installed
//                     version is 10.19.0 (`pnpm -v`).
//
//   "engines"         { "node": ">=<major>" }. Documents the minimum Node
//                     version. You're on Node 24.
//
//   "type": "module"  Makes .js files in the root (e.g. future config files) ESM.
//
//   "scripts"         Root scripts fan out to the packages. Key flags:
//                       -r / --recursive   run in every workspace package that
//                                          has that script, in dependency order
//                                          (shared before web/server)
//                       --parallel         run all at once and ignore order.
//                                          Use it for long-running `dev` watchers.
//                       --filter <name>    run in one package only
//                     Scripts you'll want:
//                       dev        → recursive + parallel "dev"
//                       build      → recursive "build"
//                       typecheck  → recursive "typecheck"
//                       test       → recursive "test"
//
//   "devDependencies" Only tools shared by the whole repo (typescript for now;
//                     vitest later). Don't type these in by hand. Run:
//                       pnpm add -D -w typescript
//                     `-w` (--workspace-root) is required to install at the root.
//                     Without it, pnpm refuses, so you don't add root deps
//                     by accident.
//
// Don't put React, Fastify, etc. here. Those go in the package that uses them.
